# ─── Secrets ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# .env holds live Supabase keys. It was NOT ignored before, which meant the
# first commit to a shared repo would have published them. Anon/publishable
# keys are designed to be exposed to browsers, but committing them still:
#   - hands anyone with repo access the project ref and key in one place
#   - makes rotation a git-history rewrite rather than a config change
#   - risks a service_role key being added to the same file later and going
#     straight into history, which would be a full database compromise
.env
.env.*
!.env.example

# ─── Dependencies & build output ──────────────────────────────────────────
node_modules
dist
dist-ssr
*.local

# Source GIF masters for the process clips (~43 MB). Kept locally so the
# transcode can be re-run, but they are not imported and must not bloat the
# repo — `npm run transcode:stages` regenerates the shipped video from them.
src/assets/stages/_gif-masters/

# ─── Tooling ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vercel
.supabase
*.tsbuildinfo
coverage

# ─── Logs ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
logs
*.log
npm-debug.log*
yarn-debug.log*
yarn-error.log*
pnpm-debug.log*
lerna-debug.log*

# ─── Editor & OS ──────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
.vscode/*
!.vscode/extensions.json
.idea
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
*.suo
*.ntvs*
*.njsproj
*.sln
*.sw?
